{"book":23,"chapter":50,"context":{"chapter":50,"title":"A Face Set Like Flint","summary":"God asks where Israel's certificate of divorce is: the exile came from their sins, not from His weakness. Then the Servant tells how he was taught morning by morning, gave his back to beatings and his face to spitting, and set his face like flint, sure that God would vindicate him.","background":"Under the Law a husband who divorced his wife gave her a written certificate (Deuteronomy 24:1), and a debtor might sell his children to pay creditors. God asks for proof that He did either. In this third Servant Song (vv. 4–11), the servant suffers precisely because he obeys.","customs":[{"term":"Plucked off the hair","verses":"50:6","note":"Pulling out a man's beard was a grave insult. David's envoys were shamed when half their beards were shaved (2 Samuel 10:4-5)."}],"watchFor":["'The tongue of the learned' is literally 'of those who are taught': the servant listens first (v. 4).","Compare v. 6 with Matthew 26:67.","'Who is he that shall condemn me?' (v. 9), echoed in Romans 8:33-34."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 24:1","Matthew 26:67","Luke 9:51","Romans 8:33-34"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["כֹּה","koh","H3541","HD","thus"],["אָמַר","'amar","H559","HVqp3ms","he says"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֵי","'ei","H335","HTi","where?"],["זֶה","zeh","H2088","HTm","this"],["סֵפֶר","sefer","H5612","HNcmsc","[is] [the] document of"],["כְּרִיתוּת","keritut","H3748","HNcfsc","[the] divorce of"],["אִמְּכֶם","'imekhem","H517","HNcfsc/Sp2mp","mother your"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["שִׁלַּחְתִּיהָ","shilachtiha","H7971","HVpp1cs/Sp3fs","I sent away her"],["אוֹ","'o","H176","HC","or"],["מִי","mi","H4310","HPi","who?"],["מִנּוֹשַׁי","minoshai","H5383","HR/Vqrmpc/Sp1bs","[is one] of creditors my"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher-","H834","HTr","whom"],["מָכַרְתִּי","makharti","H4376","HVqp1cs","I sold"],["אֶתְכֶם","'etkhem","H853","HTo/Sp2mp","<obj.> you"],["לוֹ","lo","H9033","HRd/Sp3m